Mira extensions let packages add CodeMirror behavior, preview rendering, toolbar behavior, and resolvers without tying the editor to a workspace app.

## Extension Shape

```ts
import type { MiraExtension } from "@mira-mde/extensions";

export function myExtension(): MiraExtension {
  return {
    name: "my-extension",
    codemirror: [],
    preview: {
      rehypePlugins: []
    }
  };
}
```

## Resolvers

Resolvers keep app-specific behavior outside the Markdown components.

```ts
const linkResolver = {
  resolveLink(href, context) {
    return {
      href,
      title: context.sourcePath
    };
  }
};
```

```svelte
<MiraDefaultMde {linkResolver} {assetResolver} sourcePath="notes/demo.md" />
```

## Public Entry Points

| Entry point | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- |
| `MiraMde` | Svelte editor component for custom shells. |
| `createRichEditorExtensions` | CodeMirror rich editor/live-preview behavior. |
| `createTableExtensions` | Editable table and grid-table behavior. |
| `mermaidExtension` | Mermaid rendering and live-widget support. |
| `MarkdownPreview` | Rendered Markdown surface. |
| `MiraDefaultMde` | Default editor and toolbar package. |

## Svelte

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { MiraDefaultMde } from "@mira-mde/default-ui/svelte";
  import "@mira-mde/default-ui/styles.css";

  let value = $state("# Hello Mira");
</script>

<MiraDefaultMde bind:value sourcePath="note.md" />
```

## React

```tsx
import { useState } from "react";
import { MiraDefaultMde } from "@mira-mde/react";
import "@mira-mde/react/styles.css";

export function Editor() {
  const [value, setValue] = useState("# Hello Mira");

  return <MiraDefaultMde value={value} onChange={setValue} />;
}
```

## DOM Mount

```ts
import { createMiraDefaultEditor } from "@mira-mde/default-ui";
import "@mira-mde/default-ui/styles.css";

const editor = createMiraDefaultEditor({
  root: document.querySelector("#editor")!,
  value: "# Hello Mira",
  sourcePath: "note.md"
});

editor.on("change", (markdown) => {
  console.log(markdown);
});
```

## Styles

Import one package stylesheet for the surface you use:

| Surface | Stylesheet |
| :--- | :--- |
| Svelte default UI | `@mira-mde/default-ui/styles.css` |
| React default UI | `@mira-mde/react/styles.css` |
| Lower-level Svelte editor | `@mira-mde/svelte/styles.css` |
| Rendered preview only | `@mira-mde/preview/styles.css` |

## Modes

The default editor supports `source`, `live-preview`, `preview`, and `split` modes. Feature flags can remove modes from the toolbar and prevent switching into disabled modes.

